Here's the **complete step-by-step logic** to enable real-time webhook notifications when users paste Excel/Google Sheets links into your app. This tracks **WHO edited WHAT** and pushes updates to your frontend instantly.

## 🏗️ **Complete Architecture Flow**

```
User pastes link → Your App → Setup Webhook → Cloud Excel Edit → Your Backend → Frontend Live Update
```

***

## **1. Google Sheets Implementation (Easiest)**

### **Step 1: Parse Google Sheets URL**
```javascript
// Extract sheet ID from URL
const url = "https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1ABC123xyz/edit";
const sheetId = url.match(/\/spreadsheets\/d\/([a-zA-Z0-9-_]+)/)?. [zapier](https://zapier.com/apps/google-sheets/integrations/onedrive--excel);
```

### **Step 2: Create Apps Script Webhook (Automatic)**
When user pastes link, your backend **creates this script** and deploys it:

```javascript
// YOUR_BACKEND creates this script via Google Sheets API
function setupGoogleSheetWebhook(sheetId, yourWebhookUrl) {
  const script = `
    function onEdit(e) {
      const sheet = e.source.getActiveSheet();
      const range = e.range;
      const user = Session.getActiveUser().getEmail(); // WHO edited
      const cell = range.getA1Notation();
      const oldValue = e.oldValue || '';
      const newValue = e.value || '';
      
      const payload = {
        sheetId: "${sheetId}",
        userEmail: user,
        cell: cell,
        oldValue: oldValue,
        newValue: newValue,
        timestamp: new Date().toISOString()
      };
      
      UrlFetchApp.fetch("${yourWebhookUrl}", {
        method: 'POST',
        contentType: 'application/json',
        payload: JSON.stringify(payload)
      });
    }
  `;
  
  // Create & deploy script via Google Apps Script API
  // Bind to user's sheet with their OAuth token
}
```

### **Step 3: Backend Receives Webhook**
```javascript
app.post('/google-webhook', (req, res) => {
  const { sheetId, userEmail, cell, oldValue, newValue } = req.body;
  
  // Broadcast to connected frontend clients
  io.to(sheetId).emit('cellUpdate', {
    user: userEmail,
    cell,
    oldValue,
    newValue,
    timestamp: new Date()
  });
  
  res.status(200).send('OK');
});
```

