## **2. Microsoft Excel Online (OneDrive/SharePoint)**

### **Step 1: Parse Excel URL & Get File ID**
```javascript
// Extract driveId + itemId from OneDrive URL
const url = "https://1drv.ms/x/s!ABC123?e=XYZ";
const parsed = parseOneDriveUrl(url); // Custom parser
// Returns: { driveId, itemId, fileId }
```

### **Step 2: Create Microsoft Graph Subscription**
```javascript
async function setupExcelWebhook(excelFileId, yourWebhookUrl) {
  const subscription = {
    changeType: 'updated', // Workbook changes
    notificationUrl: yourWebhookUrl, // YOUR backend
    resource: `/me/drive/items/${excelFileId}/workbook`,
    expirationDateTime: new Date(Date.now() + 24*60*60*1000).toISOString(), // 24h
    clientState: 'secretClientValue' // Security validation
  };
  
  await fetch(`https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/subscriptions`, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {
      'Authorization': `Bearer ${msGraphToken}`,
      'Content-Type': 'application/json'
    },
    body: JSON.stringify(subscription)
  });
}
```

### **Step 3: Handle Microsoft Webhook + Fetch Changes**
```javascript
app.post('/excel-webhook', async (req, res) => {
  const { resource, clientState } = req.body;
  
  if (clientState !== 'secretClientValue') return res.status(400).send('Invalid');
  
  // Microsoft webhook = change notification (no data)
  // Fetch actual changes via Graph API
  const changes = await fetchGraphChanges(resource);
  
  io.to(resource).emit('excelUpdate', changes);
  res.status(200).send('OK');
});

async function fetchGraphChanges(resource) {
  const response = await fetch(`https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0${resource}?$select=lastModifiedByUser,worksheet`, {
    headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` }
  });
  return response.json();
}
```

***

## **3. Frontend Integration Flow**

### **Step 1: User Pastes Link**
```jsx
function App() {
  const [sheetId, setSheetId] = useState('');
  
  const connectSheet = async (url) => {
    const id = parseSheetId(url); // Google or Excel
    await fetch('/api/setup-webhook', {
      method: 'POST',
      body: JSON.stringify({ url, sheetId: id })
    });
    
    // Join WebSocket room
    socket.emit('join', id);
    setSheetId(id);
  };
}
```

### **Step 2: Real-Time Updates**
```jsx
useEffect(() => {
  socket.on('cellUpdate', (update) => {
    // Highlight cell
    highlightCell(update.cell);
    
    // Show notification
    showToast(`📝 ${update.user} updated ${update.cell}: "${update.newValue}"`);
    
    // Recalculate summaries
    recalculateMetrics();
  });
}, []);
```

***

## **4. Complete Backend Setup (Node.js + Express)**

```javascript
const express = require('express');
const { Server } = require('socket.io');

const app = express();
const io = new Server();

app.use(express.json());

// 1. Setup webhook when user connects
app.post('/api/setup-webhook', async (req, res) => {
  const { url } = req.body;
  
  if (isGoogleSheets(url)) {
    await setupGoogleAppsScript(url);
  } else if (isOneDriveExcel(url)) {
    await setupMicrosoftSubscription(url);
  }
  
  res.json({ success: true, roomId: extractId(url) });
});

// 2. Receive webhooks
app.post('/webhook/google', handleGoogleWebhook);
app.post('/webhook/excel', handleExcelWebhook);

// 3. WebSocket for frontend
io.on('connection', (socket) => {
  socket.on('join', (sheetId) => {
    socket.join(sheetId);
  });
});
```

***

## **5. MVP Quick Start (Use Zapier/Pipedream for Testing)**

**No code backend needed initially:**

```
Google Sheets "New Edit" → Zapier → Your Webhook URL → Socket.io
```

**Setup:**
1. Zapier: Google Sheets → "New or Updated Spreadsheet Row"
2. Action: Webhooks by Zapier → POST to `yourapp.com/webhook`
3. Your app receives payload with user + cell data

***

## **6. User Flow Summary**

```
1. User pastes: "https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/ABC123"
2. Your app: Creates Apps Script → Deploys webhook
3. John edits B12 → Apps Script fires → POST to your backend
4. Backend: Broadcasts via Socket.io → All users see "John updated B12"
5. Frontend: Cell highlights yellow → Toast shows change → Metrics update
```

## **Key Gotchas & Solutions**

| Issue | Solution |
|-------|----------|
| Apps Script needs sheet access | Use user's OAuth token during setup |
| Microsoft subscriptions expire | Auto-renew every 24h |
| Multiple users editing | WebSocket rooms per sheetId |
| Large sheets slow | Send only changed cell diffs |
| No user email in Excel | Use Graph API `/auditEvents` |

**Start with Google Sheets** (easiest) → Add Excel later. This gives you true real-time "John edited B12: $100→$150" notifications within **3 seconds** of any edit! 🚀

